user32: Leave an already maximized window alone on SC_MAXIMIZE.

DefWindowProc handled WM_SYSCOMMAND/SC_MAXIMIZE with ShowWindow(SW_MAXIMIZE)
even when the window was maximized already, so a hidden window created with
WS_MAXIMIZE was shown and activated by it. Google Chrome does exactly this
when it restores a window that was closed maximized: it creates the browser
window hidden with WS_MAXIMIZE, and sends it SC_MAXIMIZE from Widget::Init,
before its setup is complete. The activation reaches
BrowserView::OnWidgetActivationChanged, which calls
ExtensionKeybindingRegistryViews::From(browser)->OnHostActivationChanged on
a registry not created yet: a NULL dereference (read of 0xa0) in the
browser process. Chrome 156 then crashes at every start, without a window,
until its profile no longer says maximized. Chrome runs maximized on Windows,
so Windows does not activate the window at that point.

A visible maximized window was already left as it is (ShowWindow returns
early), so only hidden maximized windows behave differently. Measured with a
test program on WinCraft 0.8.3 (Wine 11.19), after sending SC_MAXIMIZE:

  window                       before            after
  hidden, created maximized    shown, activated  hidden, not activated
  hidden, created normal       shown, activated  shown, activated
  visible, already maximized   unchanged         unchanged

With this patch, Chrome 156 starts maximized from a profile that crashed it
before, and maximize, restore, closing maximized and starting again work.

The check is made in user32, before the call into win32u, because WinCraft
can only rebuild Windows-side modules: so for an already maximized window
the WH_CBT HCBT_SYSCOMMAND hook is not called and the display driver does not
see the command. The proper fix belongs in win32u's handle_sys_command, and
the Windows behaviour should be confirmed by a conformance test run on
Windows (hidden WS_MAXIMIZE window, SC_MAXIMIZE: visible? activated?).

Status: not for WineHQ as it stands. This patch was written with an LLM,
and WineHQ does not accept LLM-generated code. No WineHQ bug describes
this yet (bugs.winehq.org searched for "chrome maximized" and SC_MAXIMIZE
on 2026-10-25).
---
--- a/dlls/user32/nonclient.c
+++ b/dlls/user32/nonclient.c
@@ -65,6 +65,10 @@ BOOL WINAPI DrawCaptionTempA (HWND hwnd, HDC hdc, const RECT *rect, HFONT hFont,
  */
 LRESULT NC_HandleSysCommand( HWND hwnd, WPARAM wParam, LPARAM lParam )
 {
+    /* An already maximized window stays as it is, even when hidden:
+     * SW_MAXIMIZE would show and activate it */
+    if ((wParam & 0xfff0) == SC_MAXIMIZE && IsZoomed( hwnd )) return 0;
+
     if (!NtUserMessageCall( hwnd, WM_SYSCOMMAND, wParam, lParam, 0, NtUserDefWindowProc, FALSE ))
         return 0;
 
